nd dynamic form of debate. It format combining the concepts of “prepared” topics with “impromptu” topics, encouraging debaters to focus on specified issues rather than debate theory or procedural arguments. This highly interactive style of debate allows debaters to engage each other, even during speeches. This challenging format requires good teamwork and in-depth quality argumentation.\nDEBATE TEAM\nMeet the BNU Debate Team\nDong Hyun Park\nDong Hyun has participated in debate since sophomore. He won several prizes and now he is the leader in BNU debate team.\nMari Ikeda\nMari has participated in International students Debate since her freshman year, and won second prize in 2011 Beijing International student debate. Outside of debate, she is studying in counseling psychology,\nAbout us\nAbout Beijing\nAbout BNU\nAbout ISO\nFamous Professors\nStudy & Life\nOrientation\nStudents Association\nFacilities\nInternship & Employment\nCopyright © 2016 Beijing Normal University. All rights reserved\nTechnical Support:\nCUCAS"
